  "worked_solution": "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=0$ the level curves are $y=\\pm 2x,$ which consists of two lines.\n\n- If $c=1$ the level curve is $4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=1,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=2$ the level curve is $2{x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\nSo, only statements I and III are true.",
